wer/id #uuid "423ef84a-8ddf-56a7-bcb1-6dee1ee8477b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "423ef84a-8ddf-56a7-bcb1-6dee1ee8477b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317780} :answer-field/id #uuid "6793789f-79bc-51ff-8ac4-da9ad114210f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318646}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44527337-615d-526b-a52d-c778cb64547f" :question/math-academy-id "q-347617" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨7-3t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(1)|?$\n\n$|{r}^{′}(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=7-3t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=-3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=2{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=4t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=4(1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93f1240f-0b47-5a56-8794-998240849da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93f1240f-0b47-5a56-8794-998240849da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318068} :answer-field/id #uuid "4162dbda-4b92-5f56-a521-c6ed9fa88ef4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76602505-6314-5889-af6f-473838f62468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76602505-6314-5889-af6f-473838f62468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317970} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae6e1aaa-dcf3-5b7d-8951-e90b6b6f06b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318803}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94125aec-27df-5037-a264-fdd046612e1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347619" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t}-4,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62183d86-51ae-5d4b-ade6-54d7ea930001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62183d86-51ae-5d4b-ade6-54d7ea930001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317898} :answer-field/id #uuid "11d6ce26-e8a6-5436-9093-81cf7c6059c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db47130-7d15-5e93-b78c-4862bf3f7ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db47130-7d15-5e93-b78c-4862bf3f7ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317662} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4110f1b-954e-5935-af00-9d4b9f7ce22c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318812}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ac22d1b-7887-5459-acc4-59652caa97eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-349469" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(0)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(0)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{2t}(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(2{e}^{2t})(t+1)+{e}^{2t}(1) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(t+1)+{e}^{2t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(0)=2{e}^{2\\cdot 0}(0+1)+{e}^{2\\cdot 0}=3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{9-{0}^{2}}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{x}^{′}(0),\\,{y}^{′}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651246de-1235-5aa2-b904-884a399472f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "651246de-1235-5aa2-b904-884a399472f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317913} :answer-field/id #uuid "b904bb26-5324-528a-bdbe-b5897385f92e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88396b9a-e2f6-58ce-9edc-0ae76c743df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88396b9a-e2f6-58ce-9edc-0ae76c743df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318027} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba08c038-5d3b-59f6-9aab-6f24fb144ce6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318829}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c81ce7cd-b6de-57e1-b7dc-68eb6562402f" :question/math-academy-id "q-349470" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4+3{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(1)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4+3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=6\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{2}+6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=12\\cdot {1}^{2}+6\\cdot 1=18.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,18⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83a93010-66f9-5f63-a619-5ae6f0ba5901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83a93010-66f9-5f63-a619-5ae6f0ba5901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318011} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b7c75a-6b0f-5c4c-82e5-e4a6e779fcee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318895}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b7b95ab-a56a-58eb-ba8d-91d73cfdc4f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-350217" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(-1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(-1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle -\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60877467-26a5-565e-9a60-7a1ac5cca6c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330808} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9e1b5e-3926-5b9a-ae3b-e6b881cd6740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330907} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc6346e-b150-5374-a32d-4d1a5ec7bc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330933} {:answer/id #uuid "86448057-4fd0-59f3-ba66-fd86d9b805be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331142} {:answer/id #uuid "d2236804-95e9-51ec-8331-608fbaf4e7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9e1b5e-3926-5b9a-ae3b-e6b881cd6740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330907} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af1f59d-cae6-5771-b8c0-f4f36400d291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332424}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf813be6-995c-5d07-9a48-ae4dc989093b" :question/math-academy-id "q-50373" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eee4af2-0248-5ce4-b7f6-6fee6d1a8fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} {:answer/id #uuid "662007e1-aa2b-54ce-b04c-f2ad08993265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330861} {:answer/id #uuid "6687452e-ac8c-536f-9456-54fd1b9619f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330866} {:answer/id #uuid "712abd91-42eb-5ec8-84bf-b6f634404a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd3b07d-2774-58fa-93e9-db174c995ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eee4af2-0248-5ce4-b7f6-6fee6d1a8fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330507} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d43db0b-4e5d-5721-97a5-e44ef07baae7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332275}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "830e243e-5841-5ab7-af4b-a130c74364b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-50409" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{\\sin }^{3}⁡t,\\,{\\cos }^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={\\sin }^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={\\cos }^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\left\\langle {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41aac7b0-e36a-52aa-883e-d2ddfd33ab74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} {:answer/id #uuid "5e338882-ec9b-52c8-9509-458d83a50da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330790} {:answer/id #uuid "8489b988-e5d3-5081-88ab-f63b44492691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331127} {:answer/id #uuid "f89ff7dc-52c8-5018-b8e3-07b4fec5c000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332135} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfbc103-aa8d-5079-8217-c29c118b141a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41aac7b0-e36a-52aa-883e-d2ddfd33ab74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22c019a-4532-5eef-bb3c-f171fa627817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332628}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90f83aed-c049-593e-9f58-73c0262de78f" :question/math-academy-id "q-50411" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\left\\langle {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fde686e-0040-50c8-9b9b-1ad4f1e8aaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392724} {:answer/id #uuid "d02ac812-19ad-5839-9ad9-16c2a59beade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392725} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ffd3e-cd2a-5031-83aa-72de86237fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392726} {:answer/id #uuid "dd140ea3-6577-5157-ab09-4fefef73b8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392727} {:answer/id #uuid "37a5973e-637b-5d29-9329-f2c326b69242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d02ac812-19ad-5839-9ad9-16c2a59beade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392725} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ef94ed-b793-5302-a468-c42ecf1df591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54" :question/math-academy-id "q-50371" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}\\right\\rangle ,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{3}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{3}-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500683} :answer-field/id #uuid "076d86ba-a029-593b-a409-24685a0fec46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500888} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c96d28-1366-5868-a326-9af707a402ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501098}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19691404-0bb9-5165-a3cc-ce9a79557b1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349464" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-7t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=3{t}^{4}-7t+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{3}-7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{3}-7,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06006b25-a443-54f2-8024-d157cc2b8a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 4t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500478} {:answer/id #uuid "4eee71c6-18a3-564f-aef0-94f6b2a849b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{1}{3t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500627} {:answer/id #uuid "67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500681} {:answer/id #uuid "da6cdfe0-793c-5d04-b91f-02dd3f4e71ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500932} {:answer/id #uuid "ff20f98e-9f1b-5ada-b97d-a2fe856607b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d97608c5-ec21-5589-b8cb-89d769aeba4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bf645e6-f706-50ea-8450-5ddbc0499160" :question/math-academy-id "q-50377" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4t-10,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500964} :answer-field/id #uuid "41888a9a-6a30-5987-80e4-7c935376e015" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500769} {:answer/id #uuid "1c11bc98-0d5a-4eaa-8520-82a30323c45b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin\\left(3t\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500769} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8c2630-d3ad-5f34-b976-b9b1cdd286bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501064}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6495e61-0973-5b35-994b-13978ddf3f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349466" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),\\,{t}^{2}+4t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{2}+4t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),\\,2t+4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c621d975-7e42-532e-8cd1-a5a95ff3741c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c621d975-7e42-532e-8cd1-a5a95ff3741c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540860} :answer-field/id #uuid "280a3379-43b0-5e7e-835c-37f28ffa4d1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdc34de8-c927-5f9c-8dbf-b5874f7e2681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdc34de8-c927-5f9c-8dbf-b5874f7e2681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540873} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d783132-2979-54b3-9fd1-5a7588deaa6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1baae25-37ff-504a-9b40-31c45e15f352" :question/math-academy-id "q-133294" :question/problem "${r}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=\\,$$⟨$\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n* For the $x$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=\\frac{5}{25+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n* For the $y$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=(\\sqrt{5})^{2}-2=3.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}),{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{6},3\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b4e2ef-e235-5e8d-a1bb-5f11c58eb2ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b4e2ef-e235-5e8d-a1bb-5f11c58eb2ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578304} :answer-field/id #uuid "37e0c65a-8bde-58ad-8512-6f5590e399eb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf1b77c6-c140-5642-9aa7-8ca14ff416d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf1b77c6-c140-5642-9aa7-8ca14ff416d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578569} :answer-field/id #uuid "626184a9-9d57-5880-91a8-6fc6755275d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578725}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0082a403-d881-57c2-9693-c2f4c2c9c358" :question/math-academy-id "q-349471" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨(t-1)({t}^{2}+2),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8-{t}^{2})⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(-1)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(-1)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=(t-1)({t}^{2}+2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(1)({t}^{2}+2)+(t-1)(2t) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)+2t(t-1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=({(-1)}^{2}+2)+2(-1)((-1)-1)=7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8-{t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{2t}{8-{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{8-{(-1)}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 7,\\,\\frac{2}{7}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e093294-73be-5e6f-93d5-92690d559de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578372} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5d3421-7483-5e3f-bccd-bdb029dfd8fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578420} {:answer/id #uuid "81d6cd8f-63d6-5870-83de-f43016f81a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578477} {:answer/id #uuid "94d011af-2fc6-571c-888c-9e4af78dd678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578511} {:answer/id #uuid "a041b31b-6075-53fd-b0a6-73ada43f50c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d6cd8f-63d6-5870-83de-f43016f81a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578477} :answer-field/id #uuid "578ac328-1776-5263-b717-611dae2652bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578722}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5571d18f-0e66-55ef-b237-25763a606307" :question/math-academy-id "q-66692" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t,\\,t{e}^{t}⟩$ what is ${r}^{′}(0)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(0)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡0=2.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=t{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}+t{e}^{t}={e}^{t}(1+t).\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)={e}^{0}(1+0)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{x}^{′}(0),\\,{y}^{′}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34408940-abbe-510e-a59c-3453e2e877f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34408940-abbe-510e-a59c-3453e2e877f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578353} :answer-field/id #uuid "56894de3-5c4e-50b7-8368-ba0533f5d21c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5bbeacb-82d4-53a1-914c-5f431020b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-349497" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle 12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t),\\,\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}\\right\\rangle ,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(2)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(2)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{12}{t},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(2)=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(2)=5(2)=10.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(2) & =⟨{x}^{′}(2),\\,{y}^{′}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(2)| & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9343e3c7-565f-57d7-9e31-6e2d178a7f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9343e3c7-565f-57d7-9e31-6e2d178a7f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578510} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e8ac0c-9c74-561e-874d-93fc85643357" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578784}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eae40ed1-ebfa-585c-ad61-ea5018bc1988" :question/math-academy-id "q-350219" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{e}^{2(t-1)},\\,-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(1)|?$\n\n$|{r}^{′}(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4{e}^{2(t-1)},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{2(t-1)},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=8{e}^{0}=8.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1),\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(1)| & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d7298e6-5173-54e9-aafb-11c1e2f77c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615617} {:answer/id #uuid "73bf58d1-395f-5411-8f03-9f9a06ac09d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\cdot ⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615782} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad8136b-84df-5709-a07c-d288fc68174e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615852} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5ff9d6-b8e3-5317-9f54-e6a9dee613db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t(1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615886} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d1f3e6-955f-54d8-9c7d-731f46d33d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\cdot ⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d1f3e6-955f-54d8-9c7d-731f46d33d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\cdot ⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615990} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7cc68a4-7fc1-51f4-97a9-54643c5bc9ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81d6ae34-be54-545c-95be-80d04c410e0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50366" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{\\tan }^{2}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={\\tan }^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t{\\sec }^{2}⁡t.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t(1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t).\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t(1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\cdot ⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,1+t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7985548a-c4b7-53b6-b316-b112f04e0e40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7985548a-c4b7-53b6-b316-b112f04e0e40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708412} :answer-field/id #uuid "14b48551-5d4e-51d2-847d-f4549783cd87" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708398} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d36a2b23-a8c4-5887-b42a-5459ef440853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d36a2b23-a8c4-5887-b42a-5459ef440853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708423} :answer-field/id #uuid "91617ac5-2a3f-5c33-85af-fef78357cbb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10ae7149-f71c-5527-b8c9-7ff98bc5cec8" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\, t^{2}\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?\n\n$r'(t)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$ {{field-2}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ x'(t) &= \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= t^{2} \\\\ y'(t) &= 2 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\langle \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\, 2 t\\rangle\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517e87e7-3201-5cca-b3c5-4ac121103b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 2 t,\\, 0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708405} {:answer/id #uuid "81d39942-8e3f-578e-9a98-ed8d68364ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708414} {:answer/id #uuid "81f6d2b9-b974-51d8-ae50-94c44330c76d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708415} {:answer/id #uuid "874a8aba-dc26-536b-86c3-6a8fa368edbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 0\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708416} {:answer/id #uuid "d5407a90-61ac-5e83-997c-05ba1cf0ae21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 2 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81f6d2b9-b974-51d8-ae50-94c44330c76d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708415} :answer-field/id #uuid "30cae4ba-4ae8-5452-832c-e2917ebb9fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708401}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3736a541-cd3c-54bf-868c-6bf078048b2f" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle \\ln{\\left(t^{2} - 4 \\right)},\\, 2 e^{3 t}\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= \\ln{\\left(t^{2} - 4 \\right)} \\\\ x'(t) &= \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= 2 e^{3 t} \\\\ y'(t) &= 6 e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0bef6a7-fa88-57e8-9de4-d9bf6d8a5fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0bef6a7-fa88-57e8-9de4-d9bf6d8a5fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708426} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bedd2d3-553b-5fd1-9c1f-ee617150cbfc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c4f3a1f-0194-5e4c-862e-fe4a26884440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{2 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c4f3a1f-0194-5e4c-862e-fe4a26884440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{2 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708407} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d092fcc-3983-5262-8644-916c6a8e8b49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708411}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6abec1ea-11ca-55b3-8bcd-65f760390e8e" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle - 6 \\sqrt{t},\\, e^{2 t} - 4\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?\n\n$r'(t)=\\langle$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$ {{field-2}} $\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - 6 \\sqrt{t} \\\\ x'(t) &= - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= e^{2 t} - 4 \\\\ y'(t) &= 2 e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}},\\, 2 e^{2 t}\\right\\rangle\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111b6f3c-6394-59a6-b507-82baed33c7fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708397} {:answer/id #uuid "20c30f32-ffbc-5909-b3db-3c5286af5835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 2 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708400} {:answer/id #uuid "433dbb32-4ab7-5c8f-b9ff-50976b3b4a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - t \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708404} {:answer/id #uuid "69179714-6814-5c53-9ce3-d4a67a9ed8ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - t \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 2 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708408} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f175e1-bead-5595-a64e-629589424372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "433dbb32-4ab7-5c8f-b9ff-50976b3b4a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle - t \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708404} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87734fb-fc18-5db0-8b3e-d354c1c4dc87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708422}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a27b20b-30fb-55ad-a802-4b35f71c18e5" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle - t \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 2 \\tan^{3}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - t \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ x'(t) &= - t \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= - 2 \\tan^{3}{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t) &= - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\langle - t \\tan{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec{\\left(t \\right)} - \\sec{\\left(t \\right)},\\, - 6 \\tan^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e19e6e6-2a09-568a-85fd-dca48ff2da45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 6 t,\\, \\frac{2 \\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right) e^{2 t} + 2 e^{4 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708399} {:answer/id #uuid "3a22e6d1-27ea-5a5f-8182-b5ec29e35b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708403} {:answer/id #uuid "89f6b493-8d70-5fea-bdec-6da3f41904ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle t^{5},\\, \\frac{2 e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708418} {:answer/id #uuid "9e97f422-da6f-51c1-a24a-9e340fac7c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle t^{5},\\, \\frac{2 \\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right) e^{2 t} + 2 e^{4 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708420} {:answer/id #uuid "da71f87f-d346-558d-ae8f-b4ed5226eaa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 6 t,\\, \\frac{2 e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a22e6d1-27ea-5a5f-8182-b5ec29e35b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708403} :answer-field/id #uuid "567619dc-a07e-5f37-9381-e545c9fbee15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708406}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "877b4c1d-ef6b-5096-9066-e22ebcacb3c7" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle t^{6},\\, \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\right\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= t^{6} \\\\ x'(t) &= 6 t^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the quotient and chain rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2} \\\\ y'(t) &= \\frac{(2 e^{2 t})(e^{2 t} + 2)-(e^{2 t})(2 e^{2 t})}{(e^{2 t} + 2)^2} \\\\ &= \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e6f85a-edd5-5b58-a2e7-8ca164e1497f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99e6f85a-edd5-5b58-a2e7-8ca164e1497f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708429} :answer-field/id #uuid "6571bb76-ff57-5e2d-9ea4-25cf3855d81a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708428}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdd98f93-2e77-5e8f-bc47-872196cc156a" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle - 2 e^{3 t - 3},\\, - 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t - 2 \\right)}\\rangle$, what is $|r'(1)|$? Give an exact answer.\n\n$|r'(1)|=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - 2 e^{3 t - 3} \\\\ x'(t) &= - 6 e^{3 t - 3} \\\\ x'(1) &= - 6 e^{-3 + 3 \\cdot 1} = -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= - 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t - 2 \\right)} \\\\ y'(t) &= - 12 \\cos{\\left(2 t - 2 \\right)} \\\\ y'(1) &= - 12 \\cos{\\left(-2 + 2 \\cdot 1 \\right)} = -12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(1)=\\langle -6,\\, -12\\rangle\n$$\n\nCompute the magnitude of the derivative vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r'(1)| &= \\sqrt{\\left(-6\\right)^2+\\left(-12\\right)^2} \\\\ &= 6 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}]}
